    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> in 1542 to replace the Lordship of Ireland, with its own parliament but the English monarch as king.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-tudor">Tudor</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-stuart">Stuart</a> wars and plantations transferred most land to Protestant settlers, and the Penal Laws excluded Catholics from power.</li><li>After winning legislative independence in 1782 and the 1798 rebellion, it was merged into the United Kingdom from 1801.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/messiah-handel">Handel’s Messiah</a> had its first performance not in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> but in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>, at the Great Music Hall on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fishamble-street">Fishamble Street</a> in April 1742.</p></aside>
    </section>

